35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows our allocation is down a quarter, and home visits earn no tariff. We must prioritize on-site care to stay solvent.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the data proves the call-back trial worked, but the system erases it. We need a program that leaves a visible, permanent record.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the staffing data is alarming. Nine nursing posts are vacant, and agency costs are rising. We cannot add burden to already stretched teams.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that’s terrifying. My findings show rooms are full by mid-morning and the car park is packed. Adding more on-site patients will just clog the system.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the space is tight, but I found the real danger. Our shared clinic closed because no one owned the rota. We must ensure clear responsibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that ownership gap is exactly why the running costs vanish. We need a model where the budget line is explicitly held by one department, not shared.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, a single owner is a trap. The trial proved the work, but the system erased it. We need a program that forces visibility, not just accountability.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree on visibility, but we must respect the staffing reality. Therapy is hemorrhaging staff, while midwifery has unexpected slack. We should leverage that specific surplus rather than straining the wards.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that slack is a lifeline! But my data shows the booking system only tracks fixed slots. If we don’t schedule these sessions, they vanish from the records entirely.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that slack is precious. But remember, our shared round lost a third of visits to simple logistics. We must plan for the messiness of real life, not just the ideal schedule.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, that slack is key. But remember, home visits earn nothing. We must use that midwifery capacity for on-site sessions to generate the revenue we desperately need.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, you’re chasing revenue while ignoring the data. The trial worked, but the system erased it. We need a program that forces visibility, not just accountability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I hear the financial urgency, but we cannot ignore the human cost. If we force midwifery into on-site revenue generation, we risk burning out the only team with capacity.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree. But if we don’t use fixed slots, the work disappears from the records. We need a structure that fits the current chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, you are right. The shared round failed because we ignored the messiness of real life. We must build in slack for the unexpected.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, I hear your frustration, but the ledger is unforgiving. We must choose a program that generates on-site revenue to cover the running costs, or it will fail.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, revenue is a byproduct, not the goal. If the work isn’t recorded, it didn’t happen. We need a program that fits the system’s rigid logic, or it will vanish like the trial.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. We must use the midwifery slack for scheduled, on-site sessions. This respects the staffing reality while ensuring the work is visible and sustainable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exactly! Scheduled slots are the only way to keep it visible. But with rooms full by mid-morning, can we actually fit these sessions without causing a bottleneck?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the rooms are tight, but the midwifery slack is real. We must schedule these sessions carefully to avoid the bottlenecks that broke our previous shared efforts.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
